INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.assessments.pass_mark',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'The score a candidate needs to pass. You can change it only while the assessment is a draft.',
  $$## Pass mark

The pass mark is the score a candidate needs to pass, from 1 to 100 percent.
It starts at the default of the level you chose. You can change it only while
the assessment is a draft. After you publish, it is locked, so every candidate
is judged by the same mark.

- **A score at the pass mark passes.** 60 percent passes a pass mark of 60.
- **Every pass earns a certificate.** A score of 90 percent or more earns
  Distinction. Any other pass earns Completion.
- **A pass mark above 90 makes Completion and Distinction the same band.**
  Every pass is then 90 percent or more, so every certificate is Distinction.
- **Old results do not change.** Each result keeps the pass mark it was judged by.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.assessments.max_attempts',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'How many times one candidate can take this assessment. Empty or 1 means one attempt.',
  $$## Attempts allowed

This is the number of times one candidate can take this assessment, from 1 to 10.
Leave it empty or set 1 for a single attempt. That is the default.

- **You can change it only while the assessment is a draft.** After you publish, it is locked.
- **A candidate sees "Attempt 2 of 3" on the start page.** After the last attempt, the result page does not offer another try.
- **Each attempt is a new test.** The timer, the questions and the answers are new for each attempt.
- **An extra attempt for one candidate is possible.** Use "Give extra attempt" in the invitations list. You must write a reason.
- **A certificate is issued once.** If a candidate passes more than once, the first certificate stays.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.assessments.score_counts',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'Which attempt counts when a candidate takes the assessment more than once: the latest or the best.',
  $$## Score that counts

This setting matters only when the assessment allows more than one attempt.

- **Latest attempt (default).** The newest attempt is the one you see in the invitations list.
- **Best attempt.** The attempt with the highest released score is the one you see.
- **Every attempt keeps its own result.** The candidate can still see each result in the results list.

You can change it only while the assessment is a draft.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.assessments.extra_attempt',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'Give one candidate one more attempt than the assessment allows. You must write a reason.',
  $$## Give extra attempt

Use this to let one candidate take the assessment one more time. It does not change the
assessment or other candidates.

- **A reason is required.** The reason is saved in the audit log with your name.
- **One press gives one attempt.** Press it again for a second extra attempt. The most is 10 extra attempts.
- **The candidate can use the same link if it is still valid.** If the link expired, use "Re-open".
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.assessments.invitations.reopen',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'Email a new link so a candidate who finished can take the next attempt.',
  $$## Re-open

Use this when a candidate finished an attempt and the assessment allows another one.

- **Only for assessments with more than one attempt.** The button appears when the candidate has an attempt left.
- **The candidate gets a new link by email.** The old link stops working. The new link is valid for 7 days.
- **No attempts left?** Use "Give extra attempt" first, then re-open.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.question_bank.pack.review',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'Open the review screen for this question set. Check each answer before candidates are invited.',
  $$## Review questions

Use this to check every question in the set, with its answer key, before you invite candidates.

- **You cannot invite candidates until the check is done.** An assessment cannot publish or send invitations while a question is In review, Needs fix or Disputed.
- **Who checks.** The super admin checks platform questions. An organisation admin checks the questions of that organisation.
- **Older questions.** Questions with the review state "Not set" still pass. They were made before the review step.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.question_bank.review.filter',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'Show only the questions in one review state.',
  $$## Review state

Pick a state to filter the list. The number in brackets is the count of questions in that state.

- **Needs review.** Questions that are In review, Needs fix or Disputed. Start here.
- **Verified.** Questions you already checked.
- **Not set.** Older questions that never entered review. They do not block an assessment.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.question_bank.review.verify',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'Mark this question as correct. The question can then go to candidates.',
  $$## Verify

Press Verify when the question, the answer key and the rationale are correct.

- **Check the key first.** A wrong key gives wrong scores to every candidate.
- **It is saved in the audit log.** The log records your name, the time and the earlier state.
- **You can change it later.** Press Needs fix if you find an error after you verify.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.question_bank.review.needs_fix',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'Flag an error in this question. You must write a note that says what to change.',
  $$## Needs fix

Use this when the question, the key or the rationale has an error.

- **A note is required.** Write what must change. The note is saved in the audit log.
- **It blocks invitations.** An assessment that holds this question cannot publish or send invitations until the question is verified.
- **Fix the question first.** Then press Verify.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.question_bank.review.withdraw',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'Take this question out of use. You cannot undo this.',
  $$## Withdraw

Use this when a question must not be used, for example because of a copyright claim.

- **The question leaves every question set** at the next sync.
- **Old attempts keep their copy.** Candidates who already took the question keep their result.
- **You cannot undo it.** A withdrawn question cannot be verified or activated again.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.question_bank.review.verify_all',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'Verify every question that is In review in this set. You see the count first.',
  $$## Verify all in this question set

Use this only after you checked the questions. The screen shows the count and asks you to confirm.

- **Only In review questions change.** Questions marked Needs fix or Disputed stay as they are.
- **The count is checked again.** If the count changed while you confirmed, nothing is saved. Review the list and try again.
- **Each question gets its own audit entry.** The log marks the entry as part of a bulk action.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.assessments.row_delete',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'Delete a test that has no attempts, or cancel a test that has attempts.',
  $$## Delete or cancel a test

Each row has one action. The action depends on whether candidates started the test.

- **Delete** removes a test that no candidate started. It also removes its invitations. You cannot undo it.
- **Cancel** retires a test that candidates started. The attempts and results stay. You cannot undo it.
- **A confirm box opens first.** It names the test and says if you can undo the action.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'admin.assessments.clear_empty_drafts',
  'admin',
  'en',
  'Delete all empty drafts in one step. An empty draft has no attempts and no invitations.',
  $$## Clear empty drafts

Use this to remove drafts you made by mistake.

- **Empty means three things.** The test is a draft, it has no attempts, and it has no invitations.
- **The box shows the count first.** You confirm before anything is deleted. You cannot undo it.
- **Other tests stay.** The server checks each test again and skips any that is not an empty draft.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
