$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.shell.nav.mobile_menu',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Open the navigation menu. Jump to Certificates, Activity, or sign out.',
  $$## Candidate navigation menu

On a phone the top bar is too narrow to show the Certificates / Activity
links inline. Tap the small handle icon on the right of the top bar to
open a dropdown menu containing:

- **Certificates** — your earned certificates.
- **Activity** — your assessment history and rankings.
- **Sign out** — end your session.

The menu closes automatically when you pick an item, when you tap
outside it, or when you press Escape. On a laptop these links appear
inline in the top bar and the handle button is hidden.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.attempt.kql.mobile_tip',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'KQL is easier on a desktop browser. Use a desktop for long queries.',
  $$## Why KQL is shown with a desktop tip on phones

The KQL question type expects you to write a structured query. Mobile keyboards lack the punctuation, operators, and pipe character that KQL uses frequently. The small viewport also makes it hard to see your full query while you write it.

You can still answer here — the textarea works the same on phone and
desktop, and your autosave runs identically. But if the question is syntax-heavy (multiple pipes, complex joins, regex), open the link on a laptop. It is much faster to answer from there.

This tip only appears on phones. On desktop you see the same editor
without the notice.
$$,
  3,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.attempt.scenario.steps',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Multi-step incident. Some steps may unlock only after submitting earlier steps.',
  $$## Scenario steps

Scenario questions describe a developing incident across multiple steps.
Each step asks for a decision or analysis given the evidence so far.

**Two modes:**

- **Free navigation** (default): jump between steps freely. You may
  revise earlier steps as later evidence arrives.
- **Locked progression**: each step unlocks only after you submit the
  previous one. Look for a small lock icon on later steps.

Once you submit a step in locked mode, you cannot edit it. In free mode
every step stays editable until you submit the assessment.

Behavioral note: AssessIQ records the order you visited the steps. There
is no "correct" order — exploring later evidence first is a valid
strategy.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.attempt.structured_case',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Read the case, then answer each step. Choose one answer or tick all that apply.',
  $$## Structured case

Read the story and the log first. Then answer each step in order.

- A round button means choose **one** answer.
- A square box means tick **all** answers that apply.
- You can change your answers until you submit the assessment.
- A step you leave blank scores 0.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.attempt.subjective.length',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Recommended 80–200 words per answer. Quality of reasoning beats word count.',
  $$## Subjective answer length

Subjective questions are graded on the rubric (key points and score bands), not on
length. A 60-word answer that nails the tradeoff scores higher than a
300-word answer that meanders.

**Rough guide:**

- **Below 40 words:** rarely enough to demonstrate reasoning.
- **80–200 words:** the sweet spot for most rubrics.
- **Above 300 words:** law of diminishing returns; you are using time
  that other questions need.

Markdown formatting (bullets, **bold**, `code`) renders in the grader's
review. Use it when it clarifies; do not use it as filler.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.attempt.disconnect',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'AssessIQ saves your answers every 5 seconds. Refresh the page and continue. The timer keeps running.',
  $$## If your connection drops

AssessIQ saves your in-progress answers to the server every 5 seconds and
shows a small green check next to "Saved" when the latest save completed.
A red dot means the last save attempt failed; AssessIQ will retry on the
next interval.

**If you lose connectivity:**

1. **The timer keeps running** — wall-clock time, not connected time.
2. **Reconnect and refresh** — your most recent autosaved state loads.
3. **Anything typed during the offline window is lost** — only saved
   state survives a refresh.

For a genuinely-blocking outage (power, hardware failure), close the tab
and contact your administrator. They can grant a one-time extension
before you submit, but cannot extend after auto-submit fires.
$$,
  2,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.attempt.navigator.toggle',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Open the question navigator. Jump to any question, see which are answered, flagged, or unseen.',
  $$## Question navigator

On a phone, the question navigator is hidden behind a small grid button
in the top bar. Tap it to open a bottom-sheet panel that shows every
question in the assessment as a numbered cell.

Cell colours mean:

- **Filled accent** — the question you are on right now.
- **Soft green** — you have entered an answer.
- **Soft amber outline** — you have flagged the question to revisit.
- **Plain outline** — you have not yet visited the question.

Tap any cell to jump straight to that question. The bottom-sheet
closes automatically after you pick. Your in-progress answer on the
current question is saved before the jump — you will not lose typing.

On a laptop the navigator is always visible on the right side of the
page and this button is hidden.
$$,
  2,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.attempt.submit.confirm',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Once submitted, you cannot reopen the attempt. Verify your flagged questions first.',
  $$## Submitting your attempt

Once you submit, your attempt is **final**. AssessIQ does not allow editing answers after
submit, and there is no second attempt unless your administrator
explicitly grants one.

Before clicking the final **Submit** button, the **Review** screen shows:

- Flagged questions you wanted to revisit.
- Unanswered questions (a blank textarea or empty MCQ counts).
- Questions whose autosave is stale (rare — usually only seconds old).

Walk through any starred or unanswered items. When you are ready, click
**Submit**. AssessIQ asks you to confirm the submit in a final dialog and the
candidate timer freezes immediately.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.submit.confirm',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Your answers are saved. You will see your result on this page or by email once it is final.',
  $$## After you submit

Your answers are saved. You will see your result on this page or by email once it is final. The timer has stopped.
There is nothing more you need to do.

- **Instant scoring.** If every question is multiple choice and your
  organisation releases results automatically, your result appears on
  this page in under a minute.
- **Otherwise** your result is emailed to your registered address, shown
  here with part of it hidden (for example `r***@gmail.com`). The message
  on this page says how long that usually takes.
- You only ever see a **complete, final** result — never a partial score
  while grading is still in progress.

If the email does not arrive, check your spam folder. You can also sign
in to the candidate portal with the same email address to see your
results.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.result.bands',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Your result shows your score, the percentage and whether you passed. You only ever see a complete, final result.',
  $$## Understanding your result

A released result shows four things:

- **Score** — the points you earned out of the total available, for
  example 42 / 60.
- **Percent** — your score as a percentage of the total.
- **Passed or Not passed** — your percentage compared with the pass mark
  set for this assessment.
- **Certificate** — if you earned one, a link to view and verify it.

A result is released only when grading is finished and final. You will
never see a partial or provisional score. Answer keys and per-question
marks are not shown.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.results.list',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Every result your organisation has released to you, newest first, with a link to any certificate you earned.',
  $$## My results

This page lists the results your organisation has **released** to you,
newest first. Each one shows your score, the percentage, whether you
passed, and a link to your certificate when you earned one.

- A result appears here only when grading is finished and it has been
  released — never earlier, and never as a partial score.
- When a result is released we also email you, with a link back to this
  page.
- If an assessment you took is missing, its result is not released yet.
$$,
  2,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.cert.share_linkedin',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Click Share on LinkedIn to post your certificate. Each share is counted in My Certificates.',
  $$## Share Your Certificate on LinkedIn

When you earn a certificate, click **Share on LinkedIn** to post it to your
LinkedIn profile. A counter records each share so you can track your
engagement in My Certificates.
$$,
  1,
