INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.auth.link_sent',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'A sign-in link is on its way. It expires in 15 minutes. If it does not arrive, wait one minute and try again.',
  $$## Check your email

A sign-in link has been sent to the address you entered. It will arrive
within a minute or two depending on your email provider.

**The link expires in 15 minutes.** If you do not click it in time, come
back to the sign-in page and request a new one.

**Did not receive anything?**

- Check your spam or junk folder.
- Make sure you entered the exact email address your administrator
  registered you with.
- Wait at least 60 seconds before requesting another link (too many
  requests in a short window are automatically rate-limited).

Each link is single-use — clicking it a second time will not work.
Request a fresh link if you need to sign in again.
$$,
  2,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.auth.session_status',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'You are currently signed in. Your session lasts 30 days from when you first clicked your sign-in link.',
  $$## Your sign-in session

You are signed in and your session is active. AssessIQ candidate sessions last **30 days** from the moment you clicked your sign-in link. You do not need to sign in again during that period.

The session is tied to this browser. If you switch to a different browser
or device you will need to request a new sign-in link.

**To sign out early**, close your browser or clear cookies. Your
certificates remain available; you just need a fresh link next time.
$$,
  2,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.auth.expiring_soon',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Your session expires in the next 5 days. Request a new sign-in link now to avoid being logged out unexpectedly.',
  $$## Your session is expiring soon

Your 30-day sign-in session will expire within the next 5 days. After it
expires you will be signed out automatically and will need to request a
new link to view your certificates again.

**To renew:** visit the sign-in page, enter your email address, and click
the link in the email you receive. Your certificates and history are not
affected — only the session changes.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.activity',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'Personal activity dashboard: completions, average score, 52-week heatmap, weekly chart and question set rankings.',
  $$## My activity

This page gives you a full picture of your assessment history on this
organisation.

### Stat cards

- **Assessments completed** — total submitted attempts in the selected period,
  broken down by subject.
- **Question sets attempted** — distinct question sets you have ever submitted
  an attempt for.
- **Avg. score** — your mean auto-graded score across all completed
  attempts in the period, with a quartile breakdown.

Use the **This week / This month / This quarter** toggle to adjust the
stats window. The heatmap and weekly chart always show the full 52-week
rolling window regardless of the toggle.

### Activity streak

The 52-week heatmap shows one cell per day. Darker cells mean more
completions on that day. The current streak counts consecutive days with
at least one submitted attempt up to and including today.

### Weekly completions

The stacked bar chart shows how many assessments you submitted each week,
coloured by subject. Hover a bar to see the exact breakdown.

### My question set rankings

One row per question set you have attempted. Shows your **best score** (the highest auto-graded result across all your attempts). It also shows your **rank** among every candidate in this organisation who took the same question set. For example
"#3 of 24" means your best score places you third out of the 24 candidates
who have submitted that question set.

Ranks are computed live and update as other candidates submit new attempts.
$$,
  3,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO help_content (id, tenant_id, key, audience, locale, short_text, long_md, version, status)
VALUES (
  gen_random_uuid(),
  NULL,
  'candidate.attempt.section',
  'candidate',
  'en',
  'This assessment has timed sections. You cannot return to a section once it is finished.',
  $$## Assessment sections

The assessment is split into sections. The timer at the top is for the **current
section** only.

- When the section timer reaches zero, your answers in that section are saved
  and locked, and the next section opens.
- Press **Finish section** to move on early. You will be asked to confirm,
  because **you cannot come back** to that section.
- The assessment ends when the last section ends, or when you submit in the last section.
$$,
  1,
  'active'
) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id, key, locale, version) DO NOTHING;

